-- title:
--   Finite and toric parts of J₁(Mp) form subgroups
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Jacobian of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring, together with a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $p$, a nonzero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ = `LaurentSeries L`, and `hK` identifies it with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, carrying an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, such that `hAp` places $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and `hζA` asserts that $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$. The element $j \in K$ satisfies `hj`: as a Laurent series it is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, and $j \neq 0$. Throughout, [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) is the two-chart model of the curve over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ attached to these data, and it is assumed proper.
--
--   **The special fibre and its two pieces.** $k$ is an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra. $C_1 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$ and $C_2 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$ (structure morphisms $c_1$, $c_2$) are proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and $i_1$, $i_2$ are closed immersions of $C_1$, $C_2$ into the base change of the two-chart model to $k$, each compatible with the structure morphisms. The hypothesis `hcover` says that every point of that base change lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` says that the scheme-theoretic intersection `pullback i₁.1 i₂.1` is reduced, and `hn`, `hn0` name its cardinality $n$ and require $n > 0$.
--
--   **Sections.** $\varepsilon$ is a section of the two-chart model over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, and $\varepsilon_1$, $\varepsilon_2$ are $k$-sections of $c_1$, $c_2$; `hε₁` requires $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ to equal the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$.
--
--   **Relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ data.** $D$ is a `RelativePic0Designation` for the two-chart model over $A$, i.e. a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism `D.toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and a zero section; `hrep` asserts that $D$ represents, relative to $\varepsilon$ and the fibrewise algebraically trivial cut `algEquivZeroCut`, the relative sub-Picard functor (a Poincaré rigidified line bundle on `D.toBase` lying in the cut, with the universal property and triviality along the zero section), while `hsm` and `hsep` require `D.toBase` to be smooth and separated. The hypothesis `hreps` is the corresponding representability statement for the base change of $D$ along $A \to k$, and `hPk` supplies an isomorphism between its Poincaré bundle and the base change of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection. Likewise $D_1$, $D_2$ with `hrep₁`, `hrep₂` represent the relative sub-Picard functors of $c_1$, $c_2$ rigidified at $\varepsilon_1$, $\varepsilon_2$.
--
--   **The map to the $C_2$-factor.** $\nu_2$ is a morphism from the base change of $D$ to $k$ to $D_2$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,k$, and `hν₂` characterises it: for every $k$-scheme $T$ and every $T$-point $a$ of the base change of $D$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` of the pullback along `curveChange i₂.1 i₂.2 t` of the pullback of `hreps.poincare` along $a$.
--
--   **The geometric fibre over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.** Algebra structures make $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` an $A$- and $L$-algebra in a scalar tower. $M_\eta$ is a `CurveModel` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (a proper smooth integral curve with an isomorphism of that field onto its function field and a bijection between closed points and places), $e_\eta$ is an isomorphism of $M_\eta.C$ with the base change of the two-chart model along $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and `heη` says that $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection is $M_\eta$'s structure morphism. The instance `Mη_chart_nonempty` requires the preimage of the finite chart to be nonempty; `hMηpin` requires, for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), that the function-field element obtained from $a$ by restriction along $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection and passage to the germ at the generic point be the coefficientwise image under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $a$ viewed in $L((q))$; and `hgal` requires the point–place dictionary `Mη.pointEquivPlace` to be equivariant for every automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ fixing $L$ pointwise, with respect to the action of [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) on places.
--
--   **The special-fibre group dictionary.** $G$ is a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9): abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus} \le G.J0s$ and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ whose kernel is $G.\mathrm{torus}$. The bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identify $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $k$-sections of the base change of `D.toBase`, of `D₁.toBase` and of `D₂.toBase`; `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` require each of these bijections to turn addition into the tensor product of the corresponding pullbacks of the Poincaré bundles; and `hproj` requires, for every $x \in G.J0s$, that `ptsI (G.proj x).1` be the composite of `pts x` with the morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` attached to $i_1$, and `ptsE (G.proj x).2` be the composite of `pts x` with $\nu_2$.
--
--   **Igusa models of the two components.** $w$ is an [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm k M`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16), and $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$, $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ are curve models over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), together with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ and $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₁`, `he₂`).
--
--   **The generic dictionary and the Abel–Jacobi data.** `gpts` is a bijection from [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186) — the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — onto the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of `D.toBase` over $A$, and `hgadd` requires it to carry addition to the relative group law of $D$ furnished by `hrep.some`. Over $L$: `hDL` is the representability statement for the base change of $D$ to $L$, `ajL` is an $L$-point-valued morphism from the base-changed curve to the base change of `D.toBase`, `kL` compares the geometric and $L$-base changes of the model (`hkL₁`, `hkL₂`), `ajbar` is a morphism $M_\eta.C \to D.P$ and $\bar\varepsilon$ a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M_\eta.C$. The hypotheses `hPL` (base-change compatibility of the Poincaré bundle over $L$), `hajLε` (`ajL` sends the base-changed section to the zero section), `hajL` (for every field $K'$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of the base-changed curve, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle along $x$ followed by `ajL` is the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the section), `hajbar` ($\mathrm{ajbar}$ is $e_\eta$ followed by $kL$, `ajL` and the first projection), `hajbar_over`, `hεbar` ($\bar\varepsilon$ is the point induced by $\varepsilon$), `hεbar_aj` ($\bar\varepsilon$ followed by $\mathrm{ajbar}$ is the zero section) and `hpts_aj` (for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x$, $s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ the point induced by $\varepsilon$, there is a degree-zero divisor equal to the difference of the places of $x$ and of $s$ whose class corresponds under `gpts` to $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajbar}$) tie the dictionary `gpts` to the Abel–Jacobi embedding.
--
--   **The place above $p$.** $\mathrm{Pl}$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hPl : Pl.LiesOverPrime p`, that is, $p$ is a nonunit of $\mathrm{Pl}$; $\rho : A \to \mathrm{Pl}$ is a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $\mathrm{Pl} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`), and $\pi_k : \mathrm{Pl} \to k$ is a surjective homomorphism with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ the structure map $A \to k$ (`hAlgk`, `hπk`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Call a class $x \in \mathrm{JOne}(Mp)$ *integral at $\mathrm{Pl}$* when there is a morphism $z$ from $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathrm{Pl}$ to $D.P$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho$ such that the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\mathrm{gpts}(x)$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathrm{Pl} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $z$. The assertion is the conjunction of eight clauses.
--
--   (1) The class $0$ is integral at $\mathrm{Pl}$.
--
--   (2) For all $x$, $x'$ and all $z$, $z'$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho$ witnessing the integrality of $x$ and of $x'$ in the above sense, there is a $z''$ witnessing the integrality of $x + x'$.
--
--   (3) For all $x$ and every witness $z$ for $x$, there is a witness $z'$ for $-x$.
--
--   (4) For all $x$, $x'$ with witnesses $z$, $z'$, there is a witness $z''$ for $x - x'$.
--
--   (5) There exist a morphism $z$ from $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathrm{Pl}$ to $D.P$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho$ and an element $y \in G.J0s$ such that $\mathrm{gpts}(0)$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Pl} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $z$, the $k$-section $\mathrm{pts}(y)$ followed by the first projection of the base change of `D.toBase` along $A \to k$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\pi_k$ followed by $z$, and $G.\mathrm{proj}(y) = 0$, i.e. $y$ lies in $G.\mathrm{torus}$.
--
--   (6) For all $x$, $x'$ and all pairs $(z, y)$, $(z', y')$ satisfying the three conditions of clause (5) for $x$ and for $x'$ respectively, there is a pair $(z'', y'')$ satisfying them for $x + x'$.
--
--   (7) For all $x$ and every pair $(z, y)$ satisfying those three conditions for $x$, there is a pair $(z', y')$ satisfying them for $-x$.
--
--   (8) For all $x$, $x'$ and all pairs $(z, y)$, $(z', y')$ satisfying them for $x$ and for $x'$, there is a pair $(z'', y'')$ satisfying them for $x - x'$.
--
--   The clauses are existence statements about witnesses, not statements that the witnesses are unique or functorially chosen.
--
--   The eight clauses say that, in the Néron-model frame for $J_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring with residue field $k$ of characteristic $p$, the set of classes integral at a chosen place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$, and the subset of those whose reduction lies in the toric part (the kernel of $G.\mathrm{proj}$, that is $G.\mathrm{torus}$), each contain $0$ and are stable under addition, negation and subtraction: they are subgroups. It serves as the group-theoretic input for the statements about Galois-equivariance of the toric reduction and about inertia acting on classes that are integral and toric at the place, which cite it.
